    code: { lang: "python", title: "secure_server.py — baseline headers on every response (complete, Python 3.10+, stdlib only)", code: "from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, HTTPServer\n\nHEADERS = {\n    'Strict-Transport-Security': 'max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains',\n    'Content-Security-Policy': \"default-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'\",\n    'X-Content-Type-Options': 'nosniff',\n    'Referrer-Policy': 'no-referrer',\n    'X-Frame-Options': 'DENY',\n    'Permissions-Policy': 'geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()',\n}\n\nclass Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def do_GET(self):\n        body = b'<h1>Lab server</h1><p>Headers do not fix apps; they fence them.</p>'\n        self.send_response(200)\n        for k, v in HEADERS.items():\n            self.send_header(k, v)\n        self.send_header('Content-Type', 'text/html; charset=utf-8')\n        self.send_header('Content-Length', str(len(body)))\n        self.end_headers()\n        self.wfile.write(body)\n    def log_message(self, *args):\n        pass  # quiet lab server\n\nprint('Serving on http://127.0.0.1:8000 — verify with: curl -I http://127.0.0.1:8000')\nHTTPServer(('127.0.0.1', 8000), Handler).serve_forever()", output: "$ curl -I http://127.0.0.1:8000\nHTTP/1.0 200 OK\nStrict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\nContent-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'\nX-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\nReferrer-Policy: no-referrer\nX-Frame-Options: DENY\n(plus the remaining headers, in server order)", lines: ["One HEADERS dict = one baseline: reviewable, diffable, reusable across apps.", "frame-ancestors 'none' in CSP is the modern clickjacking control; X-Frame-Options stays for older clients.", "HSTS over plain HTTP here is a lab artifact — browsers ignore HSTS received over HTTP; in production it is set on the HTTPS response.", "Permissions-Policy opts the page OUT of powerful features it does not use — least privilege for the browser.", "Run it with: python3 secure_server.py (then curl from a second terminal)"] },
    mistakes: ["Copy-pasting a CSP with 'unsafe-inline' and 'unsafe-eval' and calling the box ticked — the policy then permits the main XSS payload shapes.", "Setting headers on the homepage but not on error/API responses — baselines apply to every response class.", "Leaving framework debug/verbose errors on in production because 'staging needed it' — config drift is A05's engine."],
    security: "Production detection: scheduled header/config scans of YOUR OWN assets against the baseline (curl-based checks in CI), config-as-code review, and an error-page test in the regression suite (trigger a 500 on staging; the response must be generic).",
    pc: ["Run secure_server.py and curl -I it. Remove one header, restart, re-curl: your notes should catch the missing line immediately — that is a baseline check.", "Run the Level 4 header analyzer against this server and against python -m http.server; compare the two grade sheets."],
    android: ["Android's analog is the network security config: cleartext disabled, certificate pinning where appropriate, debuggable off in release — the same 'secure baseline, verified' discipline (Level 16)."],
    lab: "Guided lab: 'Security Headers Review' (Interactive Labs) — grade, then beat your own grade with this server.",
    mission: "Mission: write the deploy-gate checklist (6 items) that would have caught: debug on, default admin password, no HSTS, directory listing on, sample app deployed, verbose errors.",
